00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:04.710
tadoritsuku bashowa hitotsusa
There is only one destination

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:13.360
The Winter Traffic Safety Campaign

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:13.530
There's been a record-breaking
amount of snowfall in the Kanto area...

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:16.100
And the major transportation
services are grounded.

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:25.570
Chiikorin, our scheduled "Chief For
A Day", is stuck at the airport...

00:02:25.570 --> 00:02:27.980
So she can't make it, huh?

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:31.150
Oh, I didn't know you liked that... Chin...

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:32.710
Chiikorin!

00:02:32.710 --> 00:02:34.150
Does it matter?

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:37.620
Yes, it does! You're too old for this stuff...

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:43.390
I can't help it. The idols these days
are as young as my daughter...

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:48.190
We will cancel Chiikorin's Welcoming
and Chief Appointment Ceremony...

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:53.170
as well as the publicity work with
the Mayor. Please inform each area.

00:02:53.170 --> 00:02:58.540
We will conduct the Traffic Safety Event
with local organizations without Chiikorin.

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:01.810
Supervisors may continue to
prep the event as planned.

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:02.430
Yes, sir.

00:03:03.610 --> 00:03:04.600
Chief...

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:09.620
Should we really have the
event without Chiikorin?

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:12.090
Unfortunately, there's nothing we can do.

00:03:12.090 --> 00:03:15.020
Chiikorin won't make it here, Narasaki-kun.

00:03:15.020 --> 00:03:20.400
But we planned this event with
the condition of her being here...

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:24.560
It's not easy for me, either... How
long did I wait for this day to come?

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:31.970
Why don't we find a replacement
for her from among the residents?

00:03:31.970 --> 00:03:33.980
It'll be like a Miss Tulip contest.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:37.280
But the event is today. It's too...

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:38.410
Fine.

00:03:38.410 --> 00:03:40.620
Vice Chief, please take care of it.

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:41.550
Yes.

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:42.580
Huh?

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:00.430
Kanzato-kun?

00:04:01.070 --> 00:04:01.690
Kayano.

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:03.000
Takuro?

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:05.700
I think he's still asleep.

00:04:06.170 --> 00:04:08.670
He didn't answer when I called earlier.

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:10.070
Oh...

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:12.500
I don't blame him.

00:04:13.150 --> 00:04:14.670
He really cares for his friends.

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:19.220
Takuro and I are...

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:21.590
Don't ever draw that thing out again, okay?

00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:25.220
Persona, right? That thing?

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:29.360
We should call the police if that happens again.

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:30.470
Kayano...

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:34.440
Chiikorin is supposed to attend
an event at Kaihin Park today.

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:35.300
Huh?

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:38.440
You should take Takuro there with you.

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:39.440
Sure...

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:40.840
Where are you going?

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:41.840
To the hospital.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:43.780
Visiting my senpai.

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:46.110
Oh, that's my brother.

00:04:46.110 --> 00:04:46.950
What?

00:04:46.950 --> 00:04:49.350
He wanted to see the dormitories.

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:51.090
I'm Kanzato Jun.

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:53.760
I'm Kayano Megumi. Nice to meet you.

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:56.290
We don't look alike, huh? We get that all the time.

00:04:56.290 --> 00:04:58.860
That's not something you
should say, even if you think so.

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:00.830
You're pretty much confirming it.

00:05:00.830 --> 00:05:01.760
Oops...

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:02.600
Hey.

00:05:02.600 --> 00:05:03.930
Inui-san!

00:05:03.930 --> 00:05:05.030
Hello.

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:05.870
Wait...

00:05:05.870 --> 00:05:07.040
Wh-what is it?

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:10.270
You're not allowed to have
pets at the dorms, right?

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:13.570
R-right... but why do you ask?

00:05:19.510 --> 00:05:22.810
How am I supposed to look for one?

00:05:32.190 --> 00:05:33.320
That's...

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:37.220
Oops.

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:39.300
Detective!

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:40.270
Hey...

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:42.700
Um... where is this place?

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:46.570
Before I realized it, I was standing here.

00:05:47.110 --> 00:05:51.440
...It happens to me sometimes. Isn't it strange?

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:54.870
W-well... right...

00:05:56.320 --> 00:05:57.810
Oh, come closer.

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:02.420
You're... pretty cute.

00:06:03.520 --> 00:06:06.320
Oh, I mean, not like that.

00:06:06.490 --> 00:06:07.520
I mean...

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:09.290
Do you wanna do it today?

00:06:10.570 --> 00:06:13.230
Ah! Really, it's not like that!

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:37.630
Ayanagi Police Station
Toyama Prefecture

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:38.130
I see. That's unfortunate.

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:41.230
No, actually, I'm glad it happened.

00:06:41.230 --> 00:06:46.460
Now we have less press interviews to deal
with. I'm not too fond of celebrity events.

00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:50.710
But you know publicity work is
also an important part of your job.

00:06:50.710 --> 00:06:52.900
You shouldn't take Chiikorin so lightly.

00:06:53.610 --> 00:06:56.680
Well, that wasn't my intention.

00:06:56.680 --> 00:07:03.010
Personally, I think Hukorin is more
suitable as Chief for a Day than Chiikorin.

00:07:03.320 --> 00:07:08.250
That's just my view based on the way
she carries herself as a cosplay idol...

00:07:08.420 --> 00:07:12.760
So I'm sure others will disagree depending
on who is labeled as more niche.

00:07:12.760 --> 00:07:17.730
I wouldn't blame you if you picked
Chiikorin based on her popularity.

00:07:17.730 --> 00:07:20.100
You made the right choice.

00:07:20.230 --> 00:07:22.640
However, it wasn't my decision.

00:07:22.640 --> 00:07:28.770
Or, you could've gone with Mikorin, who's
grown popular after having throat surgery.

00:07:28.980 --> 00:07:32.910
But that would've been difficult to
arrange not knowing her recovery status.

00:07:32.910 --> 00:07:36.050
If anything, Yokorin would've
been a decent choice.

00:07:36.050 --> 00:07:38.810
Only thing is, she's already
done the Chief for a Day once.

00:07:40.590 --> 00:07:42.390
You sound like you know a lot about this.

00:07:42.590 --> 00:07:44.650
This is all common sense.

00:07:44.990 --> 00:07:46.190
Now, let's get back to business.

00:07:46.830 --> 00:07:47.620
Listen...

00:07:48.600 --> 00:07:49.860
Let me call you back.

00:07:50.500 --> 00:07:51.470
Come in.

00:07:52.970 --> 00:07:54.600
Sorry to have you come in on your day off.

00:07:54.600 --> 00:08:00.770
That's the only way to deal with this
sudden order to arbitrarily reposition.

00:08:01.340 --> 00:08:05.750
I can't guarantee I'll be of any help,
even if you place me closer to you.

00:08:05.980 --> 00:08:11.490
It was the irregular transfers due
to the expansion of the systems.

00:08:11.490 --> 00:08:13.650
I didn't use my authority to
make you come here at all.

00:08:13.650 --> 00:08:15.460
Oh, is that right?

00:08:15.460 --> 00:08:21.090
Try to stay away from me at work.
Avoid coming to this office, too.

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:24.970
Chief!

00:08:25.630 --> 00:08:29.070
I'll be temporarily positioned
here as of tomorrow by the NNIL.

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:31.040
I'm Nikaido Eiko.

00:08:31.610 --> 00:08:33.740
I'm Kubo, the Vice Chief.

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:33.810
This is the supervisor of the
Criminal Department, Ito-kun.
I'm Kubo, the Vice Chief.

00:08:33.810 --> 00:08:36.640
This is the supervisor of the
Criminal Department, Ito-kun.

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:37.710
Hello.

00:08:37.780 --> 00:08:40.850
Anyway, Chief, about our Chief for a Day...

00:08:40.850 --> 00:08:44.650
I mean, it's more like a Chief for a Half-Day now...

00:08:44.820 --> 00:08:47.480
We received a call from the office in Shintomi...

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:52.790
about a very charming girl
who just turned in a lost item.

00:08:52.790 --> 00:08:58.070
And that she seemed interested
in being the Chief for a Day...

00:08:58.070 --> 00:09:00.000
Also, Narasaki said...

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:03.830
This is Kanzato.

00:09:04.840 --> 00:09:05.930
Go ahead.

00:09:06.470 --> 00:09:08.140
Hello? What is it?

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:11.340
Really?

00:09:11.710 --> 00:09:14.450
I just spotted a man who I suspect
to be an Apathy Syndrome patient...

00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:16.420
Ahhh! He's reversing!

00:09:16.550 --> 00:09:19.110
Where are you at? I'll be there right away.

00:09:19.590 --> 00:09:22.080
I'm leaving the rest of the event up to you.

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:32.800
I said, I'm not drunk!

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:34.200
My apologies!

00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:37.240
I was ordered to report directly to you...

00:09:37.240 --> 00:09:40.640
regarding Apathy Syndrome and "Reverse" cases...

00:09:45.780 --> 00:09:47.610
What a waste of time...

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:03.320
Hey, you! What's the matter? Are you alright?

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:05.070
Ayanagi Police Station
Toyama Prefecture

00:10:05.070 --> 00:10:07.270
Ayanagi Police Station
Toyama Prefecture
What? Are you serious?
Chiikorin isn't coming anymore?

00:10:07.270 --> 00:10:07.370
Ayanagi Police Station
Toyama Prefecture

00:10:07.370 --> 00:10:08.570
Ayanagi Police Station
Toyama Prefecture
Yeah, I'm serious.

00:10:10.070 --> 00:10:11.130
Kanaru?

00:10:12.340 --> 00:10:13.570
Megumi-san...

00:10:14.510 --> 00:10:17.200
We're here to help, but...

00:10:17.710 --> 00:10:20.150
What are we supposed to-?

00:10:20.150 --> 00:10:23.950
Hmph. You two aren't too far
from looking like Chiikorin.

00:10:24.820 --> 00:10:26.880
Let's get them into wardrobe.

00:10:29.220 --> 00:10:30.250
Vice Chief!

00:10:31.160 --> 00:10:32.490
What is it?

00:10:36.100 --> 00:10:37.260
What!?

00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:43.660
Visitors?

00:10:43.840 --> 00:10:47.800
Yeah... That's what he said,
when I asked who they were.

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:53.070
"They?" So there are more
of those ridiculous people?

00:10:53.950 --> 00:10:56.780
The incident at the karaoke shop could also be...

00:10:57.220 --> 00:10:59.450
Doesn't your bro know anything?

00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:02.990
He's the Chief at Ayanagi Police Station, right?

00:11:02.990 --> 00:11:04.460
Right, yeah...

00:11:06.030 --> 00:11:08.360
I'm sure he knows something, but...

00:11:09.100 --> 00:11:12.530
Um... He's got to deal with confidentiality...

00:11:13.700 --> 00:11:16.400
Actually, we haven't even really talked.

00:11:16.740 --> 00:11:20.610
Ever since we've been back, he
doesn't tell us anything but to leave.

00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:22.430
Is that true?

00:11:22.540 --> 00:11:23.240
Yes.

00:11:23.740 --> 00:11:26.080
"Leave?" But why?

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:28.550
So... what do you think about your brother, then?

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:30.550
I don't know.

00:11:30.720 --> 00:11:32.590
You're rather dry...

00:11:32.590 --> 00:11:37.460
Oh, oops. Chiikorin is coming to Kaihin Park today.

00:11:37.590 --> 00:11:38.990
Wanna come with?

00:11:40.190 --> 00:11:43.690
We better get there early, or all
the front-row seats will be taken.

00:11:46.430 --> 00:11:49.700
I'm gonna believe that Takashi
is still alive somewhere.

00:11:51.710 --> 00:11:54.900
He might still be alive, even
if he got his Persona taken.

00:11:55.740 --> 00:11:58.540
They actually don't exist in this world anymore.

00:11:59.650 --> 00:12:02.980
I can't take it unless I kill him.

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:11.220
It's not like you saw those missing kids, right?

00:12:14.300 --> 00:12:15.260
You're right.

00:12:18.670 --> 00:12:21.940
I-I'm sorry. I got dizzy from not eating.

00:12:21.940 --> 00:12:24.960
You should take this off. You
must be suffocating in there.

00:12:25.270 --> 00:12:27.040
O-oh, no, that's...

00:12:27.040 --> 00:12:29.010
Anyone up for some takoyaki!?

00:12:29.980 --> 00:12:32.170
You're hungry, right?

00:12:32.310 --> 00:12:33.870
Hold on.

00:12:44.990 --> 00:12:46.760
Th-that was close.

00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:52.700
There's nothing we can do. He's gone.

00:12:52.700 --> 00:12:55.790
No! I want a balloon from the bear!

00:12:56.170 --> 00:12:58.760
We'll find balloons somewhere else!

00:13:00.370 --> 00:13:02.840
I don't wanna!

00:13:03.280 --> 00:13:05.610
We gathered everyone from
the Criminal Department.

00:13:05.610 --> 00:13:08.340
The ransom exchange will be
conducted two hours from now...

00:13:08.450 --> 00:13:10.310
at the Kaihin Park event hall.

00:13:10.920 --> 00:13:13.190
Please, report to the Chief quickly.

00:13:13.190 --> 00:13:13.850
Yes.

00:13:14.260 --> 00:13:15.780
I wonder if the threat is real?

00:13:16.260 --> 00:13:20.290
About killing the children and going on a
shooting spree if any officials get involved.

00:13:20.290 --> 00:13:22.420
We mustn't give in.

00:13:22.560 --> 00:13:28.630
Our top priority is to save the two sons
of the Hiiragi Pharmaceutical CEO.

00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:30.670
Let's go, already!

00:13:30.670 --> 00:13:32.640
The bear!

00:13:33.670 --> 00:13:34.640
Oh, there he is.

00:13:35.110 --> 00:13:36.470
Mr. Bear!

00:13:38.850 --> 00:13:39.780
Thank you!

00:13:45.190 --> 00:13:47.820
You know a person is inside the suit, right?

00:13:47.820 --> 00:13:49.950
That's not true! He's real!

00:13:53.390 --> 00:13:56.760
There was a call from the
culprit to President Hiiragi.

00:13:56.760 --> 00:14:04.610
The culprit claimed that he will contact
us with the final details during the event.

00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:05.400
Even if...

00:14:06.510 --> 00:14:07.840
It's a little stuffy in here...

00:14:08.340 --> 00:14:14.110
Even if you spot the culprit at the
event hall, do not make contact.

00:14:14.110 --> 00:14:17.820
Again, the safety of the hostages is our top priority.

00:14:17.820 --> 00:14:21.150
Please, follow my orders while the Chief is absent.

00:14:21.660 --> 00:14:24.490
We'll ask one of our officers to
be the Chief for a Day instead.

00:14:24.790 --> 00:14:26.930
Those two can go home now.

00:14:26.930 --> 00:14:27.590
Yes...

00:14:27.730 --> 00:14:28.890
Wait!

00:14:32.470 --> 00:14:34.260
We are gonna do this!

00:14:34.740 --> 00:14:36.700
Y-you two, how did you?

00:14:36.840 --> 00:14:39.770
We're sorry, but we were listening outside...

00:14:40.140 --> 00:14:44.200
We can't believe anyone would
kidnap little children for money!

00:14:45.080 --> 00:14:47.780
If we can be of any help...

00:14:47.780 --> 00:14:49.980
I couldn't do this alone, but
if there were two of us...

00:14:50.050 --> 00:14:51.590
Don't be stupid!

00:14:51.590 --> 00:14:54.320
But we're the chiefs for today, right?

00:14:54.590 --> 00:14:56.260
That's different from this...

00:14:56.260 --> 00:14:58.350
Let's have them help us.

00:14:59.560 --> 00:15:02.100
It would be strange if we used one of
our officers or canceled the entire event.

00:15:02.100 --> 00:15:07.600
That will just make us look more suspicious.

00:15:07.600 --> 00:15:09.400
Ito-san, but...

00:15:09.400 --> 00:15:11.870
They're underaged civilians!

00:15:12.070 --> 00:15:16.370
But, what if the culprit suspects our
movements and goes on his rampage?

00:15:18.250 --> 00:15:23.510
This is an unusual and urgent matter.
We must take all possible precautions.

00:15:24.080 --> 00:15:26.550
I don't know where he is during this time of crisis...

00:15:26.650 --> 00:15:29.780
But I think the Chief would say the same thing.

00:15:38.500 --> 00:15:40.300
He's so funny!

00:15:40.870 --> 00:15:44.330
We gotta go now, or they'll find us.

00:15:44.640 --> 00:15:47.200
Hey, you guys shouldn't just take off like that.

00:15:51.410 --> 00:15:54.870
Do you guys really know our dad?

00:15:55.220 --> 00:16:00.050
Of course. Now, come on. We'll
buy you anything you want.

00:16:03.960 --> 00:16:05.080
Tch, fine.

00:16:05.430 --> 00:16:06.260
You!

00:16:06.260 --> 00:16:07.330
Noo!

00:16:07.330 --> 00:16:08.320
Quiet down!

00:16:11.030 --> 00:16:11.620
Stop!

00:16:14.570 --> 00:16:15.300
You!

00:16:19.210 --> 00:16:21.370
Shut up!

00:16:22.680 --> 00:16:23.940
You too, come!

00:16:24.710 --> 00:16:26.210
Meekorin & Kaakorin
Chiefs of the Day

00:16:26.210 --> 00:16:27.920
Meekorin & Kaakorin

00:16:27.920 --> 00:16:28.120
Chief of the Day
U-um, everyone!

00:16:28.120 --> 00:16:30.580
Chief of the Day
Drinking and driving is bad!

00:16:30.580 --> 00:16:31.390
Chief of the Day

00:16:31.390 --> 00:16:32.650
Chief of the Day
It's against the law!

00:16:32.650 --> 00:16:34.220
Chief of the Day
If you're gonna drink, don't drive!

00:16:34.220 --> 00:16:35.620
Chief of the Day
If you're gonna drive, don't drink!

00:16:35.620 --> 00:16:35.820
If you're gonna drive, don't drink!

00:16:35.820 --> 00:16:37.830
"It won't happen to me."

00:16:37.830 --> 00:16:42.230
That kind of thinking has seen the
birth of many tragedies in the past!

00:16:42.360 --> 00:16:42.600
Don't they... look like Megumi and Morimoto?

00:16:42.600 --> 00:16:46.870
You will be charged for inciting
a driver to drink, as well!

00:16:46.870 --> 00:16:47.090
You think so?

00:16:48.700 --> 00:16:52.170
Many of us in Ayanagi City...

00:16:52.170 --> 00:16:58.080
lost loved ones from the disasters
and accidents ten years ago.

00:16:58.710 --> 00:17:07.620
As residents of this city, we should create
a lifestyle that focuses on cherishing lives!

00:17:07.620 --> 00:17:09.320
We haven't gotten any contact from the culprit.

00:17:09.460 --> 00:17:09.860
No...

00:17:09.860 --> 00:17:12.450
President Hiiragi

00:17:23.340 --> 00:17:24.570
How dare they?

00:17:25.140 --> 00:17:28.580
We will protect those two girls
with our lives, if anything happens.

00:17:28.580 --> 00:17:29.630
We know.

00:17:30.280 --> 00:17:31.010
However...

00:17:33.680 --> 00:17:36.310
That may not be necessary.

00:17:38.350 --> 00:17:39.580
Kidnapping...

00:17:40.720 --> 00:17:43.420
This is where they're gonna do the exchange...

00:17:45.630 --> 00:17:47.790
The hostages... The kids...

00:17:48.900 --> 00:17:50.890
What is your brother talking about?

00:17:52.030 --> 00:17:53.060
Shooting rampage?

00:17:56.370 --> 00:17:57.360
Be careful...

00:17:58.370 --> 00:18:00.360
These people here might be in danger.

00:18:04.010 --> 00:18:05.710
But don't use your Personas.

00:18:13.890 --> 00:18:14.910
Really?

00:18:15.690 --> 00:18:19.560
And that's all from us, the
Half-Day Chiefs, Meekorin and...

00:18:19.830 --> 00:18:21.490
Kaakorin!

00:18:25.800 --> 00:18:27.170
What? My autograph?

00:18:27.170 --> 00:18:28.660
I can't...

00:18:28.800 --> 00:18:31.210
I'll buy your CD!

00:18:31.210 --> 00:18:32.540
You two are a pair, right?

00:18:32.540 --> 00:18:34.600
Please come have an event at Akiba next time!

00:18:36.010 --> 00:18:38.910
They really do look a lot like Megumi and Morimoto.

00:18:38.910 --> 00:18:40.880
Jun, you were...

00:18:43.020 --> 00:18:47.180
Hiiragi-san, let's not give our
hopes up and wait for the culprit!

00:18:47.790 --> 00:18:50.150
I apologize, but actually...

00:18:51.990 --> 00:18:55.450
I've already done the exchange at another place...

00:18:55.830 --> 00:18:57.350
Wh-what!?

00:18:57.870 --> 00:18:59.360
Dad!

00:19:00.100 --> 00:19:02.300
Satoshi! Tsutomu!

00:19:05.610 --> 00:19:08.800
You guys are all right!

00:19:16.050 --> 00:19:17.380
Sir, this...

00:19:21.660 --> 00:19:22.710
How the-!?

00:19:23.220 --> 00:19:25.160
How did you guys make it here
without handing them this!?

00:19:25.360 --> 00:19:27.450
Mr. Bear helped us.

00:19:28.960 --> 00:19:31.260
We've taken both of them into custody.

00:19:32.270 --> 00:19:35.330
...No, they were passed out in a car.

00:19:35.600 --> 00:19:37.900
They claimed a bear attacked them...

00:20:13.470 --> 00:20:15.480
Hey, Shin, be careful.

00:20:15.480 --> 00:20:16.810
I'm fine!

00:20:26.850 --> 00:20:28.450
Look at you...

00:20:29.620 --> 00:20:30.490
Here.

00:20:34.460 --> 00:20:36.450
Let's come back tomorrow for more.

00:20:36.660 --> 00:20:37.320
Okay...

00:20:47.570 --> 00:20:50.040
Excuse me... Excuse me!

00:20:51.350 --> 00:20:53.180
Can I have one of those?

00:20:56.880 --> 00:20:58.370
If it's all right with you...

00:20:58.620 --> 00:21:00.380
I'd like the light blue one.

00:21:04.160 --> 00:21:06.090
What's with the balloon?

00:21:06.730 --> 00:21:07.960
Is it weird?

00:21:07.960 --> 00:21:09.930
Naw, rather, it suits you well.

00:21:10.760 --> 00:21:12.200
You think so?

00:21:12.400 --> 00:21:13.630
It's fine.

00:21:13.630 --> 00:21:15.330
I think it's cute.

00:21:16.240 --> 00:21:20.730
Anyway, how did you two end
up being the Chiefs for a Day?

00:21:20.970 --> 00:21:21.910
How?

00:21:21.910 --> 00:21:23.910
I found a wallet, so...

00:21:23.910 --> 00:21:25.670
I got lost, and...

00:21:26.410 --> 00:21:31.180
So, what does the real Chief do,
while the Chief for a Day is here?

00:21:32.420 --> 00:21:33.390
Who knows?

00:21:46.430 --> 00:21:53.310
Omotai kusariwo
The heavy chain

00:21:53.310 --> 00:21:59.050
ima hazushite agemashou
I will take it off for you

00:21:59.050 --> 00:22:04.380
jiyuuni naretara
Once you're free

00:22:04.380 --> 00:22:11.390
kokowo habataite yukeruwa
You'll be able to fly away

00:22:11.390 --> 00:22:17.760
atashiga samatage
I stood in your way

00:22:17.760 --> 00:22:26.210
ubatte kita madaminu sekai e
and took that world you haven't seen

00:22:26.210 --> 00:22:30.910
tamerau nonara
If you're going to hesitate

00:22:30.910 --> 00:22:39.690
huriharatte ageru sono udewo
I will free that arm for you

00:22:39.690 --> 00:22:44.260
soshite tookue
Then to faraway

00:22:44.260 --> 00:22:50.400
dekirudake tookue
As far away as possible

00:22:50.400 --> 00:22:53.670
aishiteruno
"I love you"

00:22:53.670 --> 00:22:57.400
ikanaideyo
"Don't leave me"

00:22:57.400 --> 00:23:03.970
koware chaukara
I will break

00:23:14.020 --> 00:23:16.390
Tempting breath.

00:23:16.390 --> 00:23:20.120
The gray curtain flares within a broken psyche.

00:23:20.890 --> 00:23:24.520
The girl is everywhere, but nowhere.

00:23:25.970 --> 00:23:28.300
A thought shut down long ago.

00:23:28.300 --> 00:23:31.360
But, I am within myself.

00:23:32.470 --> 00:23:36.200
Drowning in the winter sea.
Flowing with tangled sea kelp.

00:23:36.910 --> 00:23:40.370
Abdicating to never dance in the sky.
